-- title:
--   Unique transversal prime through a j=c point on the Γ₀(M') chart
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $K_0\subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the elements of [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M')`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\Gamma_0(M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, with $\varpi$ generating that maximal ideal, and with compatible algebra structures $A\to L\to K_0$. Let $j_0\in K_0$, nonzero, have Laurent expansion the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant. Write $B_0=$ `chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀`, the subalgebra of elements of $K_0$ integral over $A[j_0]$, and `jChartFin` for $j_0$ viewed in $B_0$. Fix $c\in\{0,1728\}$ and a prime ideal $x_0$ of $B_0$ containing the image of $\varpi$ and containing $j_0-c$. Then there is a prime ideal $\mathfrak{Q}_0\subseteq x_0$ of $B_0$ with $j_0-c\in\mathfrak{Q}_0$ and $\varpi\notin\mathfrak{Q}_0$ such that for every local ring $\mathcal{O}$ that is a localisation of $B_0$ at $x_0$ the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{Q}_0$ together with the image of $\varpi$ is the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$; moreover any prime ideal $\mathfrak{Q}\subseteq x_0$ containing $j_0-c$ and not containing $\varpi$ equals $\mathfrak{Q}_0$.
--
--   This is the statement that, on the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(M')$ over a discrete valuation ring of residue characteristic $q\ge 5$ prime to $M'$, the locus $j=c$ for a singular value $c\in\{0,1728\}$ passes through each of its points of the special fibre in exactly one branch, transversally to that fibre. It feeds the corresponding full-level statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_prime_map_sup_span_eq_maximalIdeal_and_isUnramifiedAt_of_map_jChartFin_mem_xH_of_isAlgebraic`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_prime_map_sup_span_eq_maximalIdeal_and_isUnramifiedAt_of_map_jChartFin_mem_xH_of_isAlgebraic), where unramifiedness of the model over $A$ at such points is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_existsUnique_prime_le_jChartFin_sub_mem_map_sup_span_eq_maximalIdeal_chartAlgFin_gamma0_of_not_dvd.lean

